A||||3||JetroGT||Parking Brake adjustment?||||1||
Z||000000||JetroGT||02-24-2001||04:07 PM||||Is their a way to adjust the parking brake? Or will I have to get new rear pads? It was working fine untill today. I took my GT to Dallas..alot of stop and go traffic. And now it's barley holding. I think the adjustment might be at the equalizer but I'm not sure.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-24-2001||06:17 PM||||You are correct, the only place to tighten or slacken the e-brakes is at the equalizer.  You'll see a nut there that you can tighten with an open ended wrench.  It is a decent size, either 15 or 17mm I think.<P><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||02-24-2001||11:02 PM||||Thanks Joe!!||||reg||14
Z||000003||tgowens||02-25-2001||12:12 PM||||yep, Joe is right - the equalizer is the adjustment. The use of the parking brake is also the way the rear brakes are adjusted. By applying the parking brake when parking it will keep your rear brakes adjusted, soooo, it MIGHT mean that it is time for new rear pads if you have too much lever travel........rather than just crawling under the car and adjusting the cable you should check the rear pads too.......||||reg||1
